/api/vendor/
/api/storage/*.key
/api/storage/phpstan/
/api/.phpunit.result.cache
/api/.phpunit.cache/

# Node / Vite
/web/node_modules/
/web/dist/
node_modules/

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json

# Docker
*.local

# Internal documentation — kept on disk, out of the repository (decision 2026-09-20).
#
# Nothing in docs/ is read at build or run time; the code only CITES these files in
# comments. The brand assets that are actually used live elsewhere and are unaffected:
# api/resources/brand/jigawa-crest.png (the PDF crest) and
# web/public/brand/jigawa-logo.png (the SPA header).
#
# Consequences, so nobody rediscovers them the hard way:
#   - A fresh clone has NO docs/. That includes docs/CLAUDE.md, which carries the
#     project's locked decisions and is cited by ~84 source files. Keep a copy
#     somewhere durable — losing your working tree loses it.
#   - The operational runbooks (DEPLOY.md, GHCR-Setup-Runbook.pdf) are therefore NOT
#     on a server checkout. scripts/deploy.sh and scripts/provision.sh no longer point
#     at them; they say where the runbooks are kept instead.
#
# To put a single file back under version control, force it past this rule:
#   git add -f docs/CLAUDE.md
/docs/
